{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "wpt-backend-4f7c-4b5e-8a3b-20260914100000",
    "name": "WPT Backend API",
    "description": "All endpoints for the WPT/ONB backend. Base path is /api/v1 (mounted in app.ts).\n\n## Setup\n1. Edit the Collection variables:\n   - `base_url` -> backend host, e.g. `http://localhost:4000/api/v1` (or `http://10.108.18.22:4000/api/v1` when testing from a phone)\n   - `phone` -> a valid E.164 test number (libphonenumber-js rejects 555-exchange numbers; use e.g. `+12125551171`)\n   - `other_phone` -> a second valid number, e.g. `+12125561172`\n   - `otp_code` -> 6-digit code shown in the backend console as `[SMS-DEV] OTP for <phone>: <code>` (no real SMS provider configured)\n   - `jwt_secret` -> value of JWT_SECRET from apps/backend/.env (needed to mint the admin token)\n   - `admin_id` -> an existing uuid from dashboard_admins (owner: `c107d002-0cee-4317-baf3-0d3b3fa63c67`)\n\n## Flow\nRun in order: Health -> Onboarding (send OTP, accept legal, verify) which stashes access/refresh tokens -> Profile -> Blocks -> Reports -> Relay -> Moderation -> Debug.\n\nNotes:\n- `/otp/verify` must come AFTER `/accept-legal` (returns 403 LEGAL_ACCEPTANCE_REQUIRED otherwise).\n- Wrong OTP codes count toward a 3-attempt lockout; verify-before-legal does not consume attempts.\n- Authenticated requests set `Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}` via a collection pre-request script. Optionally add `deviceId` from the verify response where an endpoint needs it.\n- Debug routes are triple-gated (DEBUG=1 + NODE_ENV!=production + localhost) and 404 unless enabled.\n- SMS_TWILIO_* envs are empty, so the OTP code only prints to the backend console.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:4000/api/v1" },
    { "key": "phone", "value": "+12125551171" },
    { "key": "other_phone", "value": "+12125561172" },
    { "key": "otp_code", "value": "123456" },
    { "key": "access_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "refresh_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "user_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "session_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "device_id", "value": "device_postman_test" },
    { "key": "jwt_secret", "value": "" },
    { "key": "admin_id", "value": "c107d002-0cee-4317-baf3-0d3b3fa63c67" },
    { "key": "report_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "relay_id", "value": "" }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Attach the access token to every authenticated request unless the",
          "// request already provides a token in body/pre-request.",
          "const base = pm.collectionVariables.get('base_url') || '';",
          "const token = pm.collectionVariables.get('access_token');",
          "const url = pm.request.url.toString();",
          "if (token && /\\/profile\\/|\\/blocks\\/|\\/reports\\/|\\/relay\\/|\\/session\\/check/.test(url)) {",
          "  pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Authorization', value: 'Bearer ' + token });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Collection-level helper: pm.expectStatus(pm) can be used per-request."
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
